WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.126 --> 00:00:01.505
- I got a few cousins that know

00:00:01.505 --> 00:00:03.537
their "Glow-chest-ers"
from their "Glow-sters".

00:00:03.537 --> 00:00:04.257
(buzzer buzzing)

00:00:04.257 --> 00:00:05.974
So, I think I can do this.

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:12.774
- [Voiceover] "Bill-rica."

00:00:14.056 --> 00:00:15.469
- It sounds like someone's name.

00:00:15.469 --> 00:00:16.468
- "Bill-air-ica."

00:00:16.468 --> 00:00:20.430
- It is an alternate name for America.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:23.440
- Is the double L pronounced
like a Y like in Spanish?

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.642
- "Bee-yer-ica."

00:00:24.642 --> 00:00:26.233
- How else can you
possibly pronounce this?

00:00:26.233 --> 00:00:27.857
- "Bill-rica."

00:00:27.857 --> 00:00:29.275
Then where's, there's an E there

00:00:29.275 --> 00:00:30.782
that everyone's forgetting about!

00:00:30.782 --> 00:00:33.900
- I like it better as "Bill-air-ica".

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.379
It's more patriotic.

00:00:36.161 --> 00:00:37.134
- [Voiceover] "Glaw-stir."

00:00:38.207 --> 00:00:40.315
- Like, there should be an H in here.

00:00:40.315 --> 00:00:41.400
And then I would know how to say it.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:42.339
- "Glow-sister."

00:00:42.339 --> 00:00:43.258
- "Glow-chester?"

00:00:43.258 --> 00:00:44.132
- "Glow-sister."

00:00:44.132 --> 00:00:45.382
- "Glow-chester?"

00:00:45.382 --> 00:00:46.886
- "Glow-stir."

00:00:46.886 --> 00:00:47.719
Next.

00:00:48.895 --> 00:00:50.593
- Noooooo!

00:00:50.593 --> 00:00:54.179
I've been doing it wrong this whole time.

00:00:54.179 --> 00:00:55.889
- It's "Glaw-stir", it's that simple?

00:00:56.462 --> 00:00:57.648
- [Voiceover] "Co-chich-you-it."

00:00:58.895 --> 00:00:59.851
(laughs)

00:00:59.851 --> 00:01:01.785
- This one is really hard.

00:01:01.785 --> 00:01:02.517
- What?

00:01:02.517 --> 00:01:03.689
- "Co-chee-twa-tay."

00:01:03.689 --> 00:01:04.641
- "Cotch-uh-watt-ay."

00:01:04.641 --> 00:01:05.654
- "Cuh-shis-too-ay."

00:01:05.654 --> 00:01:06.683
- "Cotch-i-twait."

00:01:06.683 --> 00:01:08.605
- Sounds like a curse word.

00:01:08.605 --> 00:01:09.943
(bleep bleep)

00:01:09.943 --> 00:01:12.444
- "Coach-i-twit?" (laughs)

00:01:12.444 --> 00:01:13.315
Wow.

00:01:13.315 --> 00:01:15.131
- Are they just trying to trick you?

00:01:16.074 --> 00:01:17.214
- [Voiceover] "Lemon-stir."

00:01:18.116 --> 00:01:19.363
- "Leo-minster?"

00:01:19.363 --> 00:01:20.252
- "Low-minster."

00:01:20.252 --> 00:01:21.625
- "La-minster."

00:01:21.625 --> 00:01:22.791
- "Lemon-stir?"

00:01:23.372 --> 00:01:24.042
- "Lemon-stir?"

00:01:24.042 --> 00:01:25.844
- What the hell happened to the O?

00:01:26.715 --> 00:01:27.558
- [Voiceover] "Lester".

00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:30.501
- What the hell?

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:32.046
There's too many E's in this word.

00:01:32.046 --> 00:01:33.013
- "Lie-stir."

00:01:33.013 --> 00:01:33.762
- "Lie-sister."

00:01:33.762 --> 00:01:34.761
- "Lee-stir."

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:35.930
- "Less-is-tur."

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:38.771
- I don't even know what
sounds letters make anymore.

00:01:38.771 --> 00:01:39.725
- "Lester?"

00:01:40.347 --> 00:01:41.149
- Nailed it.

00:01:41.149 --> 00:01:43.141
- Hold up a second.

00:01:43.141 --> 00:01:44.262
- I know someone named Lester,

00:01:44.262 --> 00:01:45.306
and that's not how it's spelled.

00:01:45.306 --> 00:01:47.934
- Why even have all these letters

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:50.663
if you're not gonna
use 'em, Massachusetts?

00:01:51.532 --> 00:01:52.446
- [Voiceover] "Hey-ver-ill."

00:01:53.689 --> 00:01:56.341
- I would say "Have-er-hill", but,

00:01:56.341 --> 00:01:58.704
by my knowledge of today,
it's probably like,

00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:01.374
it's probably just pronounced "hill".

00:02:01.374 --> 00:02:02.669
"Hah-vur-hill."

00:02:02.669 --> 00:02:03.615
- "Have-er-hill."

00:02:03.615 --> 00:02:04.757
How do you mispronounce that?

00:02:06.254 --> 00:02:09.092
- "Have-er-hill", I'm saying every letter,

00:02:09.092 --> 00:02:10.928
for the sound that the
dictionary gives it.

00:02:10.928 --> 00:02:11.842
- "Have-uh-hill?"

00:02:12.416 --> 00:02:13.226
- "Hey-vur-hill?"

00:02:14.759 --> 00:02:15.843
- Harry Potter hill?

00:02:15.843 --> 00:02:16.600
- "Hivv-er-hill."

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:17.598
- "Avril."

00:02:17.598 --> 00:02:18.810
- "Hey-ver-ill?"

00:02:19.638 --> 00:02:20.639
Oh my gosh.

00:02:20.639 --> 00:02:21.726
- Not a real word.

00:02:21.726 --> 00:02:23.896
- Either pronounce them
the way they're written,

00:02:23.896 --> 00:02:26.660
or write them differently, Massachusetts.

00:02:27.644 --> 00:02:28.566
- [Voiceover] "Wuss-ter."

00:02:29.561 --> 00:02:31.527
- This one I know because
it's like the sauce, right?

00:02:31.527 --> 00:02:33.617
"War-chest-er, War-shuss-ter" sauce?

00:02:33.617 --> 00:02:34.617
- "War-shiss-ter."

00:02:34.617 --> 00:02:35.286
- "Worse-ter."

00:02:35.286 --> 00:02:36.034
- "Wah-sister."

00:02:36.034 --> 00:02:36.960
- "Wuss-ter."

00:02:37.443 --> 00:02:38.409
Yeah.

00:02:38.409 --> 00:02:39.283
- "Wuss-ter?"

00:02:39.283 --> 00:02:40.828
- Let's ignore R's, and (bleep) it,

00:02:40.828 --> 00:02:42.411
let's ignore C's and E's too.

00:02:42.411 --> 00:02:43.701
- This is why the rest of America

00:02:43.701 --> 00:02:45.122
doesn't like to hang out with you.

00:02:45.122 --> 00:02:47.162
- (sighs) I'm never
going to Massachusetts.

00:02:47.162 --> 00:02:49.048
- I just don't know how anyone ever knows

00:02:49.048 --> 00:02:50.546
where they're going,
because if someone was like,

00:02:50.546 --> 00:02:53.292
go to "Wursh-er" or, what is it?

00:02:53.292 --> 00:02:56.012
"Wuss-ter", I would look
on the map for five hours

00:02:56.012 --> 00:02:58.346
and be like, this isn't
a place, I'm going home.

00:02:58.899 --> 00:03:02.549
- You know, did I do
my family proud today?

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:05.695
No, I did not, but...

00:03:06.928 --> 00:03:08.150
go Red Sox!

